      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`HybridFp8NvFp4Config` (the config `loader.py` builds for `nvidia/DeepSeek-V4*-NVFP4` checkpoints: FP8 attention/dense + NVFP4 routed experts) sends the FusedMoE layers that remain MXFP4 — the bundled DSpark/MTP draft experts, excluded from the NVFP4 map — to `Mxfp4FlashinferTrtllmMoEMethod` unconditionally. That TRT-LLM MoE kernel exists only on SM100. `Fp8Config.get_quant_method` already handles the identical layers of the stock checkpoint by selecting `Mxfp4FlashinferCutlassMoEMethod` on SM90/SM120 (\"SM100 uses TRT-LLM; SM90 uses W4A16 and SM120 uses MXFP8xMXFP4\"), so the hybrid path is the only place the platform branch is missing.\n\n## Modifications\n\nOne platform branch in `HybridFp8NvFp4Config.get_quant_method`, mirroring `fp8.py`: on SM90/SM120 return `Mxfp4FlashinferCutlassMoEMethod(Fp8MoEMethod(self), prefix=prefix)`; otherwise the existing TRT-LLM method. No change to the NVFP4 routed-expert method, to any non-MoE layer, or to SM100.\n\n## Accuracy / speed\n\nServed on 4× NVIDIA DGX Spark (GB10, SM121), TP4/EP4, `nvidia/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-NVFP4` @ `3431dde3`, `--moe-runner-backend flashinfer_cutlass`, DSpark block 5, `--enable-decoder-swa-bounded-replay`, on top of `e087e662` with this change bind-mounted. Without it the draft cannot load on this hardware; with it the draft loads (`Initialized DSpark draft runner ... gamma=5`) and serves:\n\n- 112/112 structured tool/JSON requests; needle retrieval exact at 131K / 262K / 655K prompt tokens; 8 concurrent 262K prompts 8/8.\n- Decode C1/C4/C8 36.9 / 80.8 / 107.4 tok/s with the draft vs 27.7 / 71.6 / 109.4 without.\n- Output is deterministic across boots (two boots gave byte-identical top-20 logprobs at 1,440 panel positions); first-token distributions identical to the no-speculation boot on the same checkpoint.\n\nFull record with raw JSON: [sparkring performance record](https://github.com/FujitsuPolycom/sparkring/blob/main/performance/records/deepseek-v41-flash/sglang-79f656a6-nvfp4-20260917.md) (§5–6). Not tested on SM90 or SM100 hardware; SM100 code path is unchanged.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] `ruff check`, `ruff format --check`, `isort --check-only --profile black` clean on the file.\n- [ ] CI.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #35336643252](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35336643252)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #35336642917](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35336642917)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #35336643182](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/35336643182)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
